# Copy to .env and edit. Docker Compose reads .env on its own, so `make`
# picks these up with no further wiring.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored — it is this machine's copy, and yours alone.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED before any command that talks to Scryfall.
#
# How this install identifies itself to the Scryfall API. Scryfall asks every
# caller to identify itself and uses this string to get in touch about its
# traffic.
#
# There is deliberately NO DEFAULT. A default would be the original
# repository's, and every fork that never read the docs would quietly send its
# requests under someone else's name — a failure invisible to the person
# causing it, landing on somebody who cannot fix it. So `make enrich` and
# `make sync-gc` refuse to run until this is set.
#
# EDIT THE LINE BELOW. Copying this file without changing it is caught and
# rejected with the same error as leaving it unset.
#
# Include a way to reach you. A repository URL is the usual choice.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCRYFALL_USER_AGENT=my-collection/1.0 (+https://github.com/you/my-collection)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. Which host address the web app is published on.
#
# Defaults to 127.0.0.1 — loopback only. The app has NO AUTHENTICATION and
# writes straight to the database, so anyone who can reach the port can edit
# your decks.
#
# 0.0.0.0 exposes it to your whole local network. That is genuinely useful for
# reading decks off a phone while sleeving, and a bad idea on a network you do
# not control. Never put it on a public address.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# APP_BIND=0.0.0.0


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing here is needed offline. `--offline`, `make rebuild`, `make validate`
# and CI never make a request, so they run with no .env at all.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
